# What must never reach the build context.
#
# Defence in depth, not the guarantee. What actually keeps credentials out of
# the image is the Dockerfile copying five named paths rather than the tree; this
# is the second line, for the day someone adds a `COPY . .`.
#
# `**/` on every pattern, because a bare `.env` is anchored at the context root
# and would miss a nested one - which is exactly the case a second line of
# defence exists for.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/storage-state.json

# Real runs. They are working data, they carry a key fingerprint and portal
# screenshots, and the hosted console serves the redacted export instead.
runs/
reviews/
**/.venv/

# Everything the console does not need at runtime.
.git/
.github/
.venv/
console/node_modules/
console/
tests/
# Named one by one rather than excluding `docs/` and adding `!docs/example-run/`
# back. Re-including a path whose parent directory is excluded is the classic
# way a .dockerignore silently drops the one thing the build needs, and this
# build cannot be run here to find out.
docs/adr/
docs/agents/
docs/research/
docs/hosting/
.scratch/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
